00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:08.410 align:start position:0%
European Union fisheries ministers have  moved closer toward wrapping up a major  reform of the e use common fishing  policy during night long talks in  brussels the ministers agreed by an  overwhelming majority on a council  position that should allow the EU irish  presidency to conclude these broad  fisheries negotiations with the european  parliament by the end of june we are now  i think and i hope on the verge of a  very very significant a final agreement  in terms of common fisheries policy  reform this is going to be a fundamental  reform in the way we fish the package is  aimed at bringing fish stocks back to  sustainable levels and providing  citizens with a safe predictable and  healthy food supply while rejuvenating  the fishing industry the ministers  agreed to take on board scientific  advice in setting rules for the  fisheries sector and to ensure that  fleet sizes match the size of fish  stocks they also committed to do away  with wasteful discards by obliging  fishermen to land all caches and  providing them with practical management  skills to do so new measures would be  introduced to for the regional  management of Fisheries  meanwhile EU farm ministers were briefed  on the latest developments in  negotiations to reform the Common  Agricultural Policy or cap with the  Parliament and Commission the talks  focused on outstanding issues like the  rules on direct payments to farmers the  requirements to be considered an active  farmer and schemes for young and small  farmers the minister's gave fresh  backing to the presidencies aims to  clinch a comprehensive political Accord  on the package with Parliament by the  end of June
 

